  {
   "id": "concept1",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "AND and OR gates"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "A logic gate is a digital circuit with one or more inputs and one output, working on two levels: 1 (HIGH) and 0 (LOW). AND gate: $Y = A\\cdot B$; output is 1 only when all inputs are 1, like switches in series. OR gate: $Y = A + B$; output is 1 when at least one input is 1, like switches in parallel. An n-input gate has $2^n$ rows in its truth table."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "AND: Y = A·B, switches in series"
    },
    {
     "en": "OR: Y = A + B, switches in parallel"
    },
    {
     "en": "Truth table rows = 2ⁿ"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "An AND gate gives one only when all inputs are one, like switches in series. An OR gate gives one when any input is one, like switches in parallel.",
    "kn": "ಆಂಡ್ ದ್ವಾರ ಎಲ್ಲಾ ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್‌ಗಳು ಒಂದಾದಾಗ ಮಾತ್ರ ಒಂದು ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಶ್ರೇಣಿ ಸ್ವಿಚ್‌ಗಳಂತೆ. ಆರ್ ದ್ವಾರ ಯಾವುದೇ ಒಂದು ಇನ್‌ಪುಟ್ ಒಂದಾದರೂ ಒಂದು ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ, ಸಮಾಂತರ ಸ್ವಿಚ್‌ಗಳಂತೆ."
   }
  },
