  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "NOT gate (inverter)"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "The NOT gate has one input and one output: $Y = \\overline{A}$. A 1 becomes 0 and a 0 becomes 1. It can be built with a transistor in CE mode: a HIGH input saturates the transistor and the output falls to about 0.2 V; a LOW input cuts it off and the output rises to $V_{CC}$."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "Y = A̅"
    },
    {
     "en": "Single input"
    },
    {
     "en": "Transistor switch acts as an inverter"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "The NOT gate simply inverts its input. A single transistor switch does this job.",
